WEBVTT

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.750
So hot...

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:07.980
It is...

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.240
We got so much summer homework.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.860
I hope we can finish it.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.420
Yeah.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.060
Want a bite?

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.300
Nah, I'm good.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:20.870
Okay.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.870
You really like ice cream, huh, Gin-chan?

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.130
Yeah, I love it.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.130
I like tea.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:37.030
Want some?

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.750
It's nice and cold.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.780
Nah.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.640
I don't like tea.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.020
I-I never knew!

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.650
I mean, tea's bitter.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.900
And it's a pain to make.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:57.180
Oh yeah, your family's 
a tea maker, isn't it?

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.720
My bad.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.380
It's just that <i>I</i> don't like it.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:01.040
Don't worry about it.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.250
All right, see you later.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.900
I'm in a bit of a hurry.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.460
I have to prepare for a move.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:11.360
M-M-Moving?! To where?!

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.050
Okay, see you, Kotsuru.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:16.050
Wait, Gin-chan!

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:19.550
No way...

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:23.810
Gin-chan's going away?

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.450
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:02:55.480 --> 00:03:00.400
<b>"I Love Ice Cream"</b>

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.420
That's nice and cold.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.880
You really don't like warm weather, huh?

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.450
All right, I've made up my mind.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:12.000
I'm not going outside 
until the summer's over.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.790
What about checking out the cafés?

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.210
I'll survive on delivery sweets.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.500
Tsubaki-kun.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.180
Come quick.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.260
This is bad.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:25.760
She says she wants to talk to you.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.530
Umm...

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:31.020
M... M...

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.270
Ma?

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:36.270
Please teach me how to 
make matcha ice c-c-c-c-cream!

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.780
<b>Rokuhoudou</b>

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:42.780
So I get that you want to teach 
that girl that tea is delicious.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.530
But why ice cream?

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:49.450
She doesn't like tea, but 
she loves ice cream.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:50.890
I see.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.800
So that's why you want 
to do matcha ice cream.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.340
Ice cream <i>would</i> make it less bitter 
and make it go down easier.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.530
Right.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.870
So I borrowed some snack 
books from the library

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.190
and tried it a few times, but...

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.110
So I thought maybe I could ask you

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:12.560
to teach me some tricks on 
making good matcha ice cream.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.410
I-I'm sorry!

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:21.150
I just realized this is a rude 
thing to ask of a professional.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.450
I don't mind, but, well...

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.630
I'll teach you the easiest recipe, then.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.660
Thank you!

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:35.420
You'll need cream, milk, eggs, and matcha.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:40.090
Cream, milk, eggs, and matcha.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.370
But do you really need to do something

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:45.300
just because your friend doesn't like tea?

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:50.180
I get that you want to convey how great 
tea is because you're a brewer's daughter,

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.240
but why do you care so much?

00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:01.110
She's moving away soon.

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:05.480
She lives with her mom,

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:09.990
and she's had to move several times
 already for her mom's work.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.500
So I want something to 
remember each other by.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:18.630
If she loves ice cream, and it helps 
her like tea even just a little,

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.420
I feel like we could stay connected, 
even when we're apart.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.900
Such a nice story.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:28.680
Sui...

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.760
You're really close, huh?

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.860
Damn it, what a pain.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.860
Can you come the day after tomorrow?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.030
It'll be easier to make it 
together than to explain it.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:00.080
<b>Closed</b>

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.080
And so,

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.520
we're making matcha ice cream today.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.260
Please and thank you, Sensei.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.470
Sure.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:13.560
All right, I'd like us to 
do a simple recipe today.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:14.710
The ingredients...

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:15.770
...are here.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:16.560
<b>Matcha ice cream (4-5 servings)</b>

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:16.560
Cream 200ml
Sugar 6 tablespoons
Milk 100ml
Matcha 1 tablespoon
3 egg yolks
<i>Loosen the matcha well.</i>

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:23.690
First, whisk the sugar and egg 
yolk well until it turns white.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:28.860
Next, warm the milk to body temperature, 
and move it into a separate bowl.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.710
Mix in the loosened matcha.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.150
Matcha tends to clump together,

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.460
so strain it after it's been mixed in.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:42.150
Blend the cream well.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:47.770
Once it stands up when you pull the blender 
out, add in the sugar and egg yolk,

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:50.230
followed by the matcha in milk.

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:52.610
Mix the whole mixture together vigorously.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.810
It's a nice color.

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.090
That looks good.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:02.040
Pour it into a container of your choice,

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.330
cool it for 4 to 5 hours, and it's done.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.640
It'll be hardened by noon.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:10.640
Come back then.

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:11.820
Okay.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.620
I look forward to it.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:15.980
I can't wait to try it.

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:18.710
Hey, can we turn down 
the temperature in the fridge?

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:19.960
Hell, no.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.930
<i>Totally left out!</i>

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:30.740
There you go.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.660
It should last for about an hour.

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:35.790
Th-Thank you.

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.160
Thank you.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.060
I'm really...

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.800
Don't worry about thanking me.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:41.810
Hurry up and take it to her.

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:43.810
Y-Yes!

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.190
I hope she appreciates it.

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:50.380
I hope it doesn't melt in the heat.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:53.120
They're meeting up at a park nearby.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.450
She's in such a hurry.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:57.360
She must be a really precious friend.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.730
Summer break.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.460
Summer break.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:06.140
It's matcha ice cream! It's summer break!

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.570
I hope Gin-chan likes it.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.970
<b>1 new message
 Gin-chan</b>

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:13.970
Gin-chan?

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:21.480
<i>Sorry, Kotsuru, there's been an accident, 
and the train's not moving.</i>

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:26.480
<b>Delay: 45 minutes
The train has been delayed 
due to an accident.</b>

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:26.480
<i>I'm at Sakurano Station right now, but
I don't know when the train's starting back up.</i>

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.730
<i>I might be a bit late.</i>

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:29.640
<i>Sorry.</i>

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:37.150
<i>Gin-chan, I'll be right there.</i>

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:40.490
<i>I wonder how long it'll take 
to get to the station.</i>

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:43.230
<i>I hope I get there before it melts.</i>

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:47.500
<i>But I can't just sit here and wait.</i>

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:51.510
<i>If you can't come to me, I'll come to you.</i>

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:52.830
<i>Right?</i>

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:56.510
<i>You've always been...</i>

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:00.320
<i>Jeez, you're such a wimp, Kotsuru.</i>

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.770
Gin-chan!

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:04.550
Come on, just a little more.

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:05.770
Hang in there, Kotsuru.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.770
Gin-chan, I'm beat!

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.510
Oh, sheesh, Kotsuru.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:13.780
Don't worry.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:18.350
If you collapse, I'll carry 
you to the finish line.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:20.730
<i>Gin-chan...</i>

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:23.150
<i>I'll be right there.</i>

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:32.800
<i>Gin-chan...</i>

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:36.050
<i>I'll be right there.</i>

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:46.560
Get on.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:53.920
U-Um...

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.320
Thank you.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.870
It's fine.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.070
It's along the way for me.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:01.580
That friend of yours...

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:02.930
Yes?

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:05.200
Like...

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.650
You said she's always moving.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:08.960
Does she have friends?

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:11.570
Not really.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:15.340
She always says what's on her mind.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.790
Everyone avoids her.

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:22.390
She's a little isolated in class, too.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.250
She's actually really kind.

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:31.900
But I love Gin-chan.

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:37.150
Hey.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.410
Gin-chan.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.160
Kotsuru.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.160
I'm so glad I got to see you.

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:52.610
Yeah, I got so bored waiting, I ran here.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:57.380
Um...

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.880
Have it before it melts.

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:04.790
What?

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:06.100
You made this?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.360
For me?

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:09.400
That's crazy.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:11.530
I thought you could handle 
it if it's ice cream.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.610
Yum!

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:17.560
Really?

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:18.790
It's not bitter?

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:22.350
It's a bit bitter, but 
that's what makes it good.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:27.960
Yeah, I never knew tea's this good.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:29.410
I had no idea.

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:33.380
What?

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.360
What's wrong?

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.030
Do you have a stomachache or something?

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:37.850
No, that's not it.

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:38.630
Then...

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:44.640
My beloved Gin-chan just said 
my beloved tea is good.

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:46.510
Kotsuru...

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:54.810
Gin-chan, let's have matcha ice cream 
together even after you switch schools.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:55.930
Huh?

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.010
I'm going to practice and get even better...

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:01.190
I'm not switching schools.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:05.360
But you said you're moving.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.200
Just to the next town.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.580
It'll be a bit far, but I'll 
be going to school from there.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:12.790
Then...

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:15.960
You totally got ahead of yourself.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.210
That's so embarrassing!

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:23.220
Oh, no, what have I done?

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:27.330
But thanks.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:30.820
Yeah.

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.830
Hey, let's make some together next time.

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:36.700
That sounds fun.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:40.100
Friends...

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.310
<i>Hey, Tsubaki-kun.</i>

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:48.300
<i>How'd Kotsuru-chan do?</i>

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.240
<i>Did she get her ice cream to her friend?</i>

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:50.740
What?

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:52.760
<i>You said you were going to the bookstore,</i>

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:56.520
<i>but you actually got worried and 
went after her, didn't you?</i>

00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:58.250
Wha— N-No!

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.910
<i>Tsubaki-kun, it's hot outside.</i>

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.010
<i>Please come home safely.</i>

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.450
<i>I'll leave the ice cream out 
so it'll be ready for you.</i>

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.640
<i>We're waiting.</i>

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:11.640
Jeez.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:19.070
Ugh, it's way too hot outside.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:25.030
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.280
Rokuhoudou.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:30.490
<b>"Vegetable Power"</b>

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:42.380
Seems like it's going to be another hot day.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:45.130
Thanks for the help.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.200
No problem.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:47.790
This is fun.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:51.470
Your home gardening gets better every year.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:52.750
Can I take those?

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:53.310
Yes.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:56.480
This year's been a huge harvest.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:58.510
A little too much so, even.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.690
I may have to do <i>that</i> thing.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.600
T-Toki-kun...

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:08.700
Don't tell me today is...

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:31.010
It's still only Thursday.

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:36.230
This is Sakurada.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.890
<i>Dad? It's me.</i>

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:41.230
Oh. Kanae.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:43.070
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:46.650
<i>I heard on TV that you got a new 
department store over there.</i>

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:47.490
Yeah?

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:50.990
<i>I'll be coming over to clean this weekend.</i>

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:53.170
Thanks.

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:54.990
You're busy, aren't you?

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.660
<i>Come on, are you really all right?</i>

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:00.310
<i>I hope you're eating.</i>

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.320
I am.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:04.180
<i>Retort-packed, I bet.</i>

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:07.010
<i>Dad...</i>

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.800
<b>Gourmet Special</b>

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:11.010
<b>Weekly Shinchou</b>

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:11.010
<i>I get that you're kind of out of it 
and bored now that you're retired,</i>

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:11.010
<b>Central Economics</b>

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:16.120
<i>but you're going to get old really quick 
if you just sit around isolated at home.</i>

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:17.270
Yeah.

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:21.540
<i>At least take a walk or 
something and get outside.</i>

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:22.770
You're right.

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:26.100
<i>Okay, Dad, see you Sunday.</i>

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:27.370
Yeah.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:28.280
<b>Japanese-style Café
 Rokuhoudou</b>

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:33.280
Outside, huh?

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.540
Hello.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:38.120
Welcome.

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:42.790
Shibano-san.

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:44.810
What's wrong?

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:46.090
I'm exhausted.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.470
It's too hot, even for me.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.120
Would you like a tempura bowl again?

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.450
Nothing too greasy.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:55.730
The summer heat's kind of got me down.

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:01.030
All right, let's have some 
lunch and get charged up.

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:02.050
Shibano-san...

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.330
Today's lunch is actually...

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:11.050
I'd like that!

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:12.450
Understood.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:19.450
<i>A white-collar worker on his own.</i>

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:22.760
<i>This place does look approachable enough.</i>

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:26.380
<i>Let's take a bit of an adventure.</i>

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:30.880
Welcome.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:36.890
<b>Today's lunches
Lunch A 
Kara-age with green onion sauce 
With rice and miso soup
 Lunch B 
With Napolitan and salad 
900 yen each</b>

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.140
<i>Lunch, huh?</i>

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:36.010
<i>Seems they have more than 
just Japanese food here.</i>

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:39.500
<i>Now, then, what should I have?</i>

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:42.640
<i>This scent...</i>

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.390
May I take your order?

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:49.150
Oh, it's not on the menu, but could it be...

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:52.440
You noticed, huh?

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:53.150
Actually...

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.420
This scent...

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:58.880
It's too good.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.660
I'm so hungry.

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:02.290
There, there.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:05.170
Just wait until lunchtime is over.

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:10.170
All right, it should be good, now.

00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:21.180
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:24.730
<i>she used to make it for me often, too.</i>

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:29.430
Thank you for waiting.

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:35.740
Our special, veggie-rich curry meal.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:41.030
Enjoy your meal.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:46.330
<i>This does look quite impressive.</i>

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:49.610
<i>It's French-fried.</i>

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:53.500
<i>This is quite appetizing.</i>

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:56.230
<i>Let's have some together.</i>

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:02.400
<i>It's good.</i>

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.830
<i>The zucchini is crisp and 
the eggplant is soft.</i>

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:08.600
<i>All sorts of textures are 
spreading through my mouth.</i>

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:12.110
<i>Okay, let's try some bell 
peppers and pumpkin together.</i>

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:24.850
<i>This is good, too.</i>

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:28.030
<i>The okra has an exciting texture, too.</i>

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:30.250
<i>It really is full of veggies.</i>

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:34.410
<i>The ground meat has an important role, too.</i>

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:36.980
<i>It brings out the uniqueness 
of each of the vegetables</i>

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:39.760
<i>while still packing its own powerful taste.</i>

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.680
<i>This really is...</i>

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:48.280
Yum!

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:51.440
S-Sorry, I couldn't help myself.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:54.340
No, it really is delicious.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:55.780
I know, right?

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:58.810
They must have some kind 
of secret ingredient.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:00.650
A secret ingredient?

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:01.930
It's tomato.

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:06.540
We added some fresh-picked 
tomato into the roux.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:11.460
It makes it rich, and the 
lycopene is a good antioxidant.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.710
It's perfect when you're beat from the heat.

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:18.350
I see, I can believe it.

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:18.780
Right?

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:20.350
Y-Yeah.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:21.090
I agree.

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:24.310
I was so beat today.

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:26.570
But see? I'm all better now.

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:28.220
I'm pumped up.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.530
<i>Curry, huh?</i>

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:32.040
I'm ready to take on the world.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:36.200
I'm going to finish the day on time today 
and come back for the tempura bowl tonight.

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:39.000
We'll be waiting with your 
double chicken tempura bowl.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:40.600
Oh, did you know?

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:42.870
The tempura bowl here is ridiculously good.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.170
The chicken tempura bowl
is especially awesome.

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:49.240
Thank you.

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:54.590
Was the curry to your liking?

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:57.630
That meal's only available 
during the summer.

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:00.260
We look forward to it every year, too.

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:02.070
Yeah.

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:05.600
It's really fancy, and yet it 
manages to taste nostalgic.

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.470
I haven't had hand-made 
curry in a long time.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.560
I'm glad to hear.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.150
My wife...

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:17.730
I lost my wife a little while ago.

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:24.490
Oh, you know, you don't really 
make curry when you're alone.

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:28.280
I'm used to being by myself now, but y'know.

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:31.380
There's just not enough 
excitement in my life.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:38.740
But it's nice going out to do 
something every now and then.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.800
I haven't had such a fun day in a while.

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:46.890
I had something that I could 
honestly say I enjoyed.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.340
Sir...

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:56.830
Please come back whenever you'd like.

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:59.780
Feel free to stop by, even 
if just for a cup of coffee.

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.360
We'll be waiting.

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.210
Thanks.

00:21:10.820 --> 00:21:15.430
Tomato, ground meat, carrots, onions...

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:18.160
I still have rice.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:24.650
<i>It won't be as good as hers, but...</i>

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:35.930
<i>Maybe I'll make Kanae some curry on Sunday.</i>

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:41.070
Well, then.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.950
Time to eat.

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:30.340
<b>Next episode</b>

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:30.340
<b>"Espresso Espressivo"</b>

00:23:15.840 --> 00:23:19.130
Why is curry so good on the 
day after it's been made?

00:23:19.130 --> 00:23:23.870
That's because the umami seeps out of the 
ingredients and makes it richer, I heard.

00:23:23.870 --> 00:23:25.660
Just the same as people.

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:29.180
The more time you spend, the more 
depth you discover in them.

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:30.340
<b>Come again soon.</b>
